{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|_|and|_|intransitive}} To be a member of a vessel's crew
#: {{ux|en|We '''crewed''' together on a fishing boat last year.}}
#: {{ux|en|The ship was '''crewed''' by fifty sailors.}}
# To be a member of a work or production crew
#: {{ux|en|The film was '''crewed''' and directed by students.}}
# To [[supply]] workers or sailors for a crew
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1997|title=Cod|author=Mark Kurlansky|page=182|text=The seafood companies '''crewed''' huge trawlers with new fishermen, many of whom were fish-plant workers, since much of the work on board a modern trawler is fish processing.}}
